{
  "about": "The functions admitted after ADR-0047's first list (docs/specs/exsheet-functions, ticket 01): what ExcelCases cannot state, Linked Tables, recalculation, and a text past a cell's limit. Transcribed from ExSheet.Engine.Tests' FunctionAdditionTests.",
  "kind": "sheet",
  "culture": "en-US",
  "setups": {
    "declared": [
      {"declareTable": {"name": "Rates", "columns": ["Pair", "Mid"]}}
    ],
    "pushed": [
      {"declareTable": {"name": "Rates", "columns": ["Pair", "Mid"]}},
      {"pushTable": {"name": "Rates", "rows": [["EURUSD", 1.08], ["USDJPY", null]]}}
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: a function that answers about any Value never answers about data that has not arrived: =IFNA(Rates[Mid],0)",
      "setup": "declared",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "=IFNA(Rates[Mid],0)"}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: a function that answers about any Value never answers about data that has not arrived: =ISBLANK(INDEX(Rates[Mid],1))",
      "setup": "declared",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "=ISBLANK(INDEX(Rates[Mid],1))"}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: a function that answers about any Value never answers about data that has not arrived: =ISNUMBER(INDEX(Rates[Mid],1))",
      "setup": "declared",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "=ISNUMBER(INDEX(Rates[Mid],1))"}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: a function that answers about any Value never answers about data that has not arrived: =NOT(INDEX(Rates[Mid],1))",
      "setup": "declared",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "=NOT(INDEX(Rates[Mid],1))"}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: a function that answers about any Value never answers about data that has not arrived: =AND(Rates[Mid])",
      "setup": "declared",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "=AND(Rates[Mid])"}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: a function that answers about any Value never answers about data that has not arrived: =CONCAT(Rates[Pair])",
      "setup": "declared",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "=CONCAT(Rates[Pair])"}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: INDEX reads a Linked Table's column by position, and a missing Value is blank",
      "setup": "pushed",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=INDEX(Rates[Mid],1)", "B2": "=ISBLANK(INDEX(Rates[Mid],2))", "B3": "=INDEX(Rates[Mid],3)"}, "expect": {"values": {"B1": 1.08, "B2": true, "B3": {"error": "#REF!"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0047: INDEX's range is a dependency, so a change inside it recomputes the Formula",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "1", "A2": "2", "B1": "=INDEX(A1:A3,2)"}},
        {"enter": {"A2": "5"}, "expect": {"values": {"B1": 5}, "change": {"recalculated": ["B1"]}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: CONCAT past a cell's 32767 characters is #VALUE!, never a cut text",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "", "A2": "", "A3": "c", "B1": "=LEN(CONCAT(A1:A2))", "B2": "=CONCAT(A1:A3)"}, "expect": {"values": {"B1": 32767, "B2": {"error": "#VALUE!"}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =AND()",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=AND()"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =NOT(TRUE,FALSE)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=NOT(TRUE,FALSE)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =IFNA(1)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=IFNA(1)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =ROUNDUP(1)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=ROUNDUP(1)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =MOD(1)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=MOD(1)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =DATE(2026,1)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=DATE(2026,1)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =EOMONTH(1)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=EOMONTH(1)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =LEFT()",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=LEFT()"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =MID(\"a\",1)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=MID(\"a\",1)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "docs/specs/exsheet-functions: a call with the wrong number of arguments is refused, as Excel does: =INDEX(A1:A2)",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B1": "=INDEX(A1:A2)"}, "expect": {"throws": {"refusal": "formulaSyntax"}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ticket 04: ROW() and COLUMN() read their own cell's place, so a move recalculates them though their text is unchanged",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"B2": "=ROW()*100+COLUMN()"}, "expect": {"values": {"B2": 202}}},
        {"do": {"insertRows": [0]}, "expect": {"values": {"B3": 302}}},
        {"do": {"insertColumns": [0, 2]}, "expect": {"values": {"D3": 304}}}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
